<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José Joaquín de Olmedo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1780">1780</a>–<a href="/years/1847">1847</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José Joaquín de Olmedo was an Ecuadorian poet and statesman who wrote the ode La victoria de Junín in honour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guayaquil">Guayaquil</a> threw off Spanish rule on 9 October 1820 he headed the government of the Free Province of Guayaquil until Bolívar annexed it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Gran</a> Colombia in 1822. He later became vice-president of Ecuador.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-joaquin-de-olmedo.jpg" alt="José Joaquín de Olmedo" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: El Universo (pintor desconocido) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jjolemdo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
